# Authentication middleware and identity

## Plugin semantics

Authentication runs in the middleware queue (before controllers). Controllers/components read the identity from the request/authentication result per plugin conventions.

## Required behavior

- Place Authentication middleware according to official docs and existing `Application::middleware` order.
- Use project patterns for `allowUnauthenticated` / public actions.
- Access identity through the installed plugin’s request/identity APIs — inspect neighboring controllers first.
- Prefer middleware for cross-cutting authn gates over ad-hoc controller checks that re-implement login.

## Anti-patterns

- Re-checking credentials in every action instead of middleware/service
- Assuming session vs JWT authenticator without reading project config
